# module:  hermes
# toggle:  agents.hermes
# summary: Hermes — NousResearch general-purpose ASSISTANT (memory, chat, local Ollama).
# Distinct from the coding agents; included deliberately. NOT Hermes-Function-Calling/Atropos.
#
# SPIKE FINDING: the official installer is curl|bash. Run as ROOT with --non-interactive →
# FHS layout: binary linked at /usr/local/bin/hermes, code at /usr/local/lib/hermes-agent
# (system paths → survive the runtime profile mount). Per-tenant data lives in ~/.hermes
# (config wizard / hermes-config.yaml on first entry). The installer vendors its own Python
# via uv. Needs >= 64K context for tool use; llm_server injects OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH from the
# flavor's model.context_length (131072 on the reference machine — comfortably over 64K).
#
# PINNED. The earlier note here said the installer had no version-pin flag; that is wrong — it
# takes `--commit SHA` (and `--dir`). Without it every dev_base rebuild silently produced a
# different hermes, which is the one thing an immutable image is supposed to prevent.
#
# The SHA below MUST match `agents.hermes.pin` in setup/schema/sources.yaml — that file is the
# single place versions are chosen, and validate.sh fails if the two drift apart. Bump both
# together. This layer is the floor a fresh box starts from; `uu update agents` installs the
# same pinned commit into the shared tree without needing a rebuild.
RUN curl -fsSL https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/install.sh -o /tmp/hermes-install.sh \
 && bash /tmp/hermes-install.sh --non-interactive \
      --commit 3b9a963b8e5cdb804a422755bed9a60fcd778273 </dev/null \
 && rm -f /tmp/hermes-install.sh \
 && test -x /usr/local/bin/hermes
